description:
[narrowed from route-edit-93a8ab50] In repos/activity-api/src/routes/execution-traces.ts, in the region "Idempotence marker on the AUTHORITATIVE row", widen the reach grading guard so an execution whose verdict tag was already written can still have its posterior updated.

THE DEFECT, measured on the live substrate. The reach endpoint grades an execution's posterior only when the row's pre-existing tags classify as ungraded. But the verdict tag is written to the row before that check runs, so once a row carries a reached false tag the classifier returns not-reached rather than ungraded, the guard falls through, and the posterior is never updated. The row ends up holding an honest verdict that no arm ever learns from. Counted right now for the compose arm: one thousand and ninety four rows carry no tags at all, thirty three carry a reached false tag with no grading stamp, and only seven carry the reach graded marker that means the posterior actually moved. That arm's alpha and beta have not changed in ten hours while thirty four not reached verdicts accumulated on its rows.

WHY THE EXISTING DOUBLE-COUNT PROTECTION IS ENOUGH. The same condition already tests that the row does not carry the reach graded true marker, and that marker is written inside this branch precisely as an idempotence stamp before the credit is applied. That marker alone is the correct guard against grading the same execution twice. Requiring the pre-verdict to be ungraded on top of it is what strands a row whose verdict tag was written first, because the presence of a verdict is being read as evidence that the posterior was already updated, which is not the same thing and is false on this path.

Perform exactly one replacement. Find the sole occurrence of this line:
      if (preVerdict === 'ungraded') {

Replace it with these lines:
      // A row whose verdict tag was written before this check classifies as
      // 'not-reached' or 'reached', not 'ungraded' — and requiring 'ungraded'
      // here stranded it permanently: the verdict existed and no posterior ever
      // moved. Measured on feature_compose: 33 rows held a reached:false tag with
      // no reach_graded:true stamp while alpha/beta sat unchanged for ten hours.
      // The reach_graded:true marker tested in the enclosing condition is the
      // real double-count guard; it is written inside this branch before credit
      // is applied, so honouring a verdict that is already known cannot double
      // count. 'ungraded' still grades as before — this only stops discarding a
      // verdict the walk has already reported.
      if (preVerdict === 'ungraded' || preVerdict === 'not-reached' || preVerdict === 'reached') {

Everything inside the branch is unchanged, including the idempotence marker write that immediately follows. The enclosing condition, which already excludes satellites and rows carrying reach_graded:true, is untouched.

One replacement, one file, inside the named region. Change nothing else.

